    "summary": {
      "candidates": [
        {
          "evidence": [
            {
              "locator": "section:lead",
              "original_text": "EDU war eine private höhere Bildungseinrichtung, die 2018 in Kalkara (Malta) gegründet wurde, jedoch dort nicht als Universität registriert war, und ein Onlinestudium für internationale Studenten im Fach Medizin anbot.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:lead",
              "original_text": "Am 23. November 2023 wurde in Malta ein Antrag beim Civil Court (Commercial Section) zur Auflösung und Abwicklung der Trägergesellschaft eingereicht.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Allgemeines",
              "original_text": "Sie war bis zum 26. Juni 2024 als „Higher Education Institution“ lizenziert.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Allgemeines",
              "original_text": "Trägerin war die Digital Education Holdings Ltd.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:lead",
              "original_text": "Das Studium sollte zu den Abschlüssen Bachelor of Medicine (B.Med.) und Master of Medicine (MMed) führen.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Studium",
              "original_text": "jeweils 10 Wochen englischsprachiger Online-Fernunterricht für die theoretischen Inhalte und anschließend vier Wochen praktischer Unterricht in einem Lehrkrankenhaus in der Landessprache stattfand.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Studium",
              "original_text": "Im November 2018 begann man mit acht Studierenden.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Studium",
              "original_text": "Nach eigenen Angaben waren im Mai 2023 97 Studierende immatrikuliert.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Anerkennung_des_Abschlusses",
              "original_text": "Im Februar 2021 stellte die maltesische Akkreditierungsbehörde MFHEA klar, dass die Akkreditierung des Studienprogramms noch nicht bedeute, dass die Absolventen den Beruf als Arzt ausüben dürften.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Anerkennung_des_Abschlusses",
              "original_text": "Im Februar 2020 wurde zur Qualitätssicherung eine Kooperation der EDU mit der Faculty of Health, Medicine and Life Sciences (FHML), einer Institution der Universität Maastricht vereinbart.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Allgemeines",
              "original_text": "Bachelor of Education – Early Childhood (180 ECTS)\nBachelor of Medicine (180 ECTS)\nMaster of Medicine (120 ECTS)\nPhilosphical Doctorate",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "c1",
          "value": {
            "language": "en",
            "text": "EDU was a private higher education institution established in 2018 in Kalkara, Malta, offering online medical education to international students. It was licensed as a higher education institution rather than registered as a university. The licence described in its institutional history ran until 26 June 2024. Its operator was Digital Education Holdings Ltd.; an application to dissolve and wind up that company was filed in Malta on 23 November 2023. This corporate proceeding is distinct from the institution’s original establishment and educational licence.\n\nThe medical programme was designed to lead to Bachelor of Medicine and Master of Medicine qualifications. Its format combined English-language online theoretical instruction with practical teaching in hospitals in the local language. Teaching began with eight students in November 2018, and EDU reported 97 enrolled students in May 2023. The relationship between educational accreditation and professional registration remained a significant issue: accreditation of the study programmes did not itself guarantee recognition as a qualification permitting medical practice. In February 2020, EDU agreed a quality-assurance cooperation with the Faculty of Health, Medicine and Life Sciences at Maastricht University. Its accredited programme list also included early-childhood education and a doctoral programme."
          },
          "verification": "supported"
        }
      ],
      "preferred": {
        "candidate_id": "c1",
        "reason_code": "only_available"
      }
    }
